dcomp: do not copy a same-process swap chain into the window it already presents to

Ableton Live 12.4.16 and Topaz Photo 1.7.1 (app list batch 1): the dcomp bridge read back every
frame of the app's own window swap chain (CreateSwapChainForHwnd) on its 16 ms thread -- copy to a
staging texture, Map (waits for the GPU), StretchDIBits into the window's GDI surface. DXVK already
presents that chain into the window's Vulkan client surface, which winewayland shows ABOVE the GDI
surface (it is placed below only with NEUTRON_DCOMP_SUPPRESS_CLIENT=1, which nothing sets), so the
copy lands underneath where nobody sees it. Premiere, After Effects, Media Encoder and Audition never
paid it (NEUTRON_DCOMP_NATIVE=1); Photoshop, Illustrator, Animate, Lightroom Classic, InDesign and
every program did.

Windows: a swap chain made for a window reaches the screen through that window; DWM composes it and
nothing copies it elsewhere. The bridge now leaves a same-process chain alone when its DXGI desc
OutputWindow is the registered window itself (windowed) and the client surface is not suppressed.
Composition chains (OutputWindow NULL: Qt alpha windows, WebView2, CEF) and every window of another
process still go through the bridge, which is how they reach the screen. Registration, the
__wine_dcomp_blit mark and the bounded-acquire stamp are unchanged.

Not covered / not checked: Illustrator, Animate, Lightroom Classic, InDesign, and earlier programs
(CapCut, Filmora, FL Studio, VSDC, vMix, Affinity, Cavalry). A window whose Vulkan client surface is
not shown (none found) would lose the copy that showed under it: NEUTRON_DCOMP_HWND_CHAIN_COPY=1.

Lab (11.10-182d, 30 s windows, app process CPU of one core): Live (welcome dialog over the main
window) 15.8% / 29.7%, 0 readbacks, 2 of 2; NEUTRON_DCOMP_HWND_CHAIN_COPY=1 on the same build
61.8% / 59.1%, 2,358 / 2,458 readbacks. Topaz sign-in screen 57.6% / 56.8% vs 77.6% / 76.3%.
Both draw the same in every run. Photoshop 2026: Home and the opened Chepino Valley document drawn,
the document pixel-identical (0 px) to the run with this switch off; Premiere 2026 Home + Waterfalls
project drawn (Premiere is NEUTRON_DCOMP_NATIVE, unaffected).

Applies after dcomp-flip-discard-buffer0 (same file). Kill switch NEUTRON_DCOMP_HWND_CHAIN_COPY=1.

--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
@@ -403,6 +403,32 @@
     return 0;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON 2026-11-05: a swap chain created for a window (CreateSwapChainForHwnd) reaches the screen through
+ * that window on Windows -- DWM composes it, nothing copies it anywhere else. DXVK presents it into the
+ * window's own Vulkan client surface, which winewayland shows above the window's GDI surface (unless
+ * NEUTRON_DCOMP_SUPPRESS_CLIENT=1 hides it for the bridge). The bridge nevertheless read back every frame of
+ * such a chain in the app's own process and StretchDIBits'd it into that GDI surface, underneath, where
+ * nobody sees it: Ableton Live 12 spent 62-68% of a core with the copy and 20% without it, Topaz Photo
+ * 81% and 62% (lab, 11-05). Composition swap chains (no window of their own: DXGI desc OutputWindow is
+ * NULL) and windows of another process still go through the bridge, which is how they reach the screen.
+ * Kill switch NEUTRON_DCOMP_HWND_CHAIN_COPY=1 (copy them again). */
+static BOOL neutron_hwnd_chain_direct(IDXGISwapChain *swapchain, HWND hwnd)
+{
+    static int copy = -1, suppress = -1;
+    DXGI_SWAP_CHAIN_DESC scd;
+
+    if (copy < 0)
+    {
+        char b[8];
+        copy = (GetEnvironmentVariableA("NEUTRON_DCOMP_HWND_CHAIN_COPY", b, sizeof(b)) && b[0] == '1') ? 1 : 0;
+        suppress = (GetEnvironmentVariableA("NEUTRON_DCOMP_SUPPRESS_CLIENT", b, sizeof(b)) && b[0] == '1') ? 1 : 0;
+        ERR("neutron-gateresolved: NEUTRON_DCOMP_HWND_CHAIN_COPY = %d (suppress_client %d)\n", copy, suppress);
+    }
+    if (copy || suppress || !hwnd) return FALSE;
+    if (FAILED(IDXGISwapChain_GetDesc(swapchain, &scd))) return FALSE;
+    return scd.OutputWindow == hwnd && scd.Windowed;
+}
+
 /* NEUTRON bounded-acquire handshake (round 32). Private DXVK interface --
  * must match INeutronBoundedAcquire in dxvk's dxgi_interfaces.h. We stamp
  * every swapchain we readback-blit so DXVK bounds its otherwise-infinite WSI
@@ -1228,7 +1254,7 @@
     IDXGISwapChain *swapchain = NULL;
     struct presentation *p;
     HWND host, target;
-    BOOL target_cross_proc = FALSE;
+    BOOL target_cross_proc = FALSE, hwnd_direct;
 
     if (!hwnd || !content)
         return;
@@ -1399,6 +1425,9 @@
         }
     }
 
+    /* NEUTRON 2026-11-05: a same-process swap chain made for this very window is on screen already. */
+    hwnd_direct = !target_cross_proc && target == hwnd && neutron_hwnd_chain_direct(swapchain, hwnd);
+
     InitOnceExecuteOnce(&presentations_once, presentations_init, NULL, NULL);
 
     EnterCriticalSection(&presentations_cs);
@@ -1408,7 +1437,7 @@
         {
             p->present_hwnd = target;
             p->cross_proc = target_cross_proc;
-            p->no_blit = (neutron_dcomp_native() && !target_cross_proc); /* round-35 native */
+            p->no_blit = (neutron_dcomp_native() && !target_cross_proc) || hwnd_direct; /* round-35 native */
             /* NEUTRON M4: this function is the per-Present hook -> mark a blit pending so
              * the 16ms blit thread only reads back windows that actually presented. */
             InterlockedExchange(&p->pending_blit, TRUE);
@@ -1440,7 +1469,7 @@
         p->hwnd = hwnd;
         p->present_hwnd = target;
         p->cross_proc = target_cross_proc;
-        p->no_blit = (neutron_dcomp_native() && !target_cross_proc); /* round-35 native */
+        p->no_blit = (neutron_dcomp_native() && !target_cross_proc) || hwnd_direct; /* round-35 native */
         p->swapchain = swapchain; /* take QI ref */
         p->content_id = content; /* NEUTRON M4: fast-path identity */
         p->pending_blit = TRUE; /* NEUTRON M4: fresh present -> blit once */
